&& L1 CLEANUP -- retire the spec-minted live heads so no future run ADOPTS them.
&& AIF-078 lifecycle lane, step L1. Owner-authorized 2026-08-27.
&&
&& THIS WRITES TO THE PRODUCTION CATALOG. Backup taken first at
&& tmp/catalog_backup/WORKSPACES.{dbf,dtx}.20260827T230621Z
&&
&& WHAT IT DOES AND DOES NOT DO. WORKSPACE DELETE flags a name's rows AND sets
&& SUPERSEDED. Adoption is stopped by SUPERSEDED, not by the flag -- the verb
&& says so itself. Nothing is packed: the rows stay on disk, stay readable
&& under SET DELETED OFF, and the max(WS_ID)+1 high-water is preserved because
&& the allocator still counts them.
&&
&& IT FLAGS THE WHOLE CHAIN, NOT JUST THE LIVE HEAD. These names have been
&& running since 2026-08-11, so 110 of 252 rows carry them. Visible rows drop
&& from 216 to 106. That was measured and shown to the owner before this ran.
&&
&& SEVEN LIVE HEADS ARE DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE:
&&   mcc_x64, mcc_v3, sess_cursor, mcc_db, mcc_minidb_memo -- real saved
&&     workspaces, not spec residue.
&&   x64, x32 -- DIRECTORY IDENTITIES. `workspace open dbf` ADOPTING these is
&&     the D10.1 feature working as designed, not a defect. Retiring them would
&&     break the thing the lane built.
&&
&& PREDICTIONS ARE WRITTEN DOWN BEFORE THE RUN, per house discipline. Each
&& DELETE's reported row count is predicted inline; their sum must equal the
&& drop in visible COUNT (216 - 106 = 110).

ECHO === BEFORE ===
&& AMENDED 2026-08-28: the hardcoded D:\code\ccode path is gone. It was
&& OI-017's shape living in this lane's own tooling -- a TRACKED script that
&& cannot run for anyone who clones. `&_WORKSPACES` is the engine-owned
&& variable (fd0d6ef40): it resolves the WORKSPACES slot AT EXPANSION TIME, so
&& this reads whatever catalog is actually in force. Run bare it reads
&& production; run under an AIF-078 L2 bracket it reads the scratch root, which
&& is the correct answer to "census the catalog I am using" in both cases.
USE &_WORKSPACES\WORKSPACES.dbf
COUNT
COUNT FOR SUPERSEDED = "0"
&& predict: 216 visible, 21 live heads

ECHO === the fourteen, one per line so each row count is visible ===
WORKSPACE DELETE partialprobe
&& predict 1
WORKSPACE DELETE goneprobe
&& predict 1
WORKSPACE DELETE goneprobe2
&& predict 1
WORKSPACE DELETE cycle_from_ram
&& predict 1
WORKSPACE DELETE v3_regress
&& predict 12
WORKSPACE DELETE LADDERTEST
&& predict 1
WORKSPACE DELETE lsfall
&& predict 1
WORKSPACE DELETE ls_probe
&& predict 11
WORKSPACE DELETE ls_idxprobe
&& predict 11
WORKSPACE DELETE wm_regress
&& predict 14
WORKSPACE DELETE sess_regress
&& predict 9
WORKSPACE DELETE ram_hydrate_src
&& predict 14
WORKSPACE DELETE minidb_regress
&& predict 17
WORKSPACE DELETE minidb_sidecar
&& predict 16

ECHO === AFTER -- visible rows and live heads ===
USE &_WORKSPACES\WORKSPACES.dbf
COUNT
COUNT FOR SUPERSEDED = "0"
&& predict: 106 visible, 7 live heads

ECHO === NOTHING WAS PACKED -- the rows are still on disk ===
SET DELETED OFF
COUNT
&& predict 252, unchanged

ECHO === and the allocation high-water is intact ===
GO BOTTOM
? WS_ID
&& predict 252
SET DELETED ON

ECHO === the seven that remain, by name ===
LIST ALL FOR SUPERSEDED = "0"
